    "q-109196": {
      "dom_id": "step-q109196",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the rectangle $C$ in the plane with vertices $(0,1),(0,-1),(1,-1)$ and $(1,1),$ and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ According to Green's theorem, \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,dx-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\,dy={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nCalculate the function $f(x,y).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14223852/assets/a3e81cfacc47dfa241a5fea64de84e375a58a6d86ceab82c86303763d5e41fe5.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-2y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,dx-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[-2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-(-2y)]\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2y(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x,y)=2y(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-109196-a",
